<title>ITALY: Gross yields rise at Italian BTP bond auction.</title>
<headline>Gross yields rise at Italian BTP bond auction.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Auction results for a third tranche of 2.0 trillion lire worth of three-year Italian Treasury fixed rate bonds (BTPs) with a 6.00 percent coupon, and a first tranche of 3.0 trillion lire of 6.25 percent May 15, 2002 BTPs.</p>
<p>		  May 15, 2000   pvs	May 15, 2002   pvs</p>
<p> Net Yield	 5.78 pct    5.45	  6.04 pct    5.71</p>
<p> Gross Yield     6.57 pct    6.24	  6.90 pct    6.56</p>
<p> Assigned price 98.75	 99.60	 97.75	 99.15</p>
<p> Bids	     4.430 trln lire	   5.290 trln lire</p>
<p> Assigned	 2.000 trln lire	   3.000 trln lire</p>
<p>Note - The three-year BTP comparisons are with a previous auction on May 16. The five-year BTP comparisons are with an 11th tranche of March 1, 2002 paper.</p>
</text>
